                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 22 at 6:35PM EDT until August 23 at 12:00AM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, northern, northwest, and western\nVirginia, including the following areas, Albemarle, Central\nVirginia Blue Ridge, Greene, Orange, Culpeper, Madison, Northern\nVirginia Blue Ridge, Page, Rappahannock, Shenandoah, and\nRockingham.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight EDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Several rounds of slow moving showers and thunderstorms are\nexpected to move across Central Virginia and parts of the\nShenandoah Valley through late this evening. Around 1 to 3\ninches of rain have already fallen in parts of the Watch\narea. Additional rain amounts of 2 to 4 inches are likely for\nsome locations, with isolated higher totals possible if\nthunderstorms become stalled.\n- Please visit www.weather.gov/safety/flood for flood safety\nand preparedness information",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
